From 0722632953ddc42463419344ccea805067535bc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 07:13:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] microblaze: Tell the libm tests that soft-float has no
 exceptions or rounding modes

MicroBlaze uses ieee754/soft-fp and the generic <bits/fenv.h>, which
defines no FE_* exception macros and only to-nearest rounding, with
the generic stub fesetround.  Nothing told the libm test harness, so
test_exceptions in math/libm-test-support.c found no exception class
to test and hit "assert (ran == 1)" in every libm test that checks
exceptions: 933 of the math tests abort with SIGABRT on a cross build
run under qemu-user.

Add the same math-tests-exceptions.h and math-tests-rounding.h that
the arc, riscv, loongarch and or1k nofpu configurations use.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sysdeps/microblaze/math-tests-exceptions.h | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 sysdeps/microblaze/math-tests-rounding.h   | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 54 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sysdeps/microblaze/math-tests-exceptions.h
 create mode 100644 sysdeps/microblaze/math-tests-rounding.h

diff --git a/sysdeps/microblaze/math-tests-exceptions.h b/sysdeps/microblaze/math-tests-exceptions.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..5d7c129238
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sysdeps/microblaze/math-tests-exceptions.h
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+/* Configuration for math tests: exception support.  MicroBlaze version.
+   Copyright (C) 2026 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
+   This file is part of the GNU C Library.
+
+   The GNU C Library is free software; you can redistribute it and/or
